\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Input component spectra before TDI and clock correction. The measured electronic residual and sideband-difference estimator are plotted without smoothing over $0.25\,\mathrm  {mHz}$--$1\,\mathrm  {Hz}$. The calculated carrier and sideband readout use the operating point of Table~\ref {tab:readout_components}, including ideal ADC quantization. The dashed curve is the single-link OMS-plus-acceleration comparison. This existing input plot does not yet include the proposed $15\,\mathrm  {MHz}\,A_\epsilon $ timing scale. The board treatment in the existing output plot is discussed in Section~\ref {sec:electronic_noise}.}}{13}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:component_inputs_single_link}{{3}{13}{Input component spectra before TDI and clock correction. The measured electronic residual and sideband-difference estimator are plotted without smoothing over $0.25\,\mathrm {mHz}$--$1\,\mathrm {Hz}$. The calculated carrier and sideband readout use the operating point of Table~\ref {tab:readout_components}, including ideal ADC quantization. The dashed curve is the single-link OMS-plus-acceleration comparison. This existing input plot does not yet include the proposed $15\,\mathrm {MHz}\,A_\epsilon $ timing scale. The board treatment in the existing output plot is discussed in Section~\ref {sec:electronic_noise}}{figure.3}{}}
